  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Okinawan sanshin-and-eisa music of the Ryukyu archipelago (southwestern Japan), historically and culturally distinct from mainland Japanese music. The sanshin (Okinawan three-string snake-skin-bellied long-neck plucked lute, the direct ancestor of the mainland shamisen) anchors the melodic content of solo-and-ensemble Okinawan classical (kunkunshi-notated court music), folk min'yō, and the contemporary popular Okinawan-pop forms. Eisa is the Okinawan summer Bon-festival ancestor-honoring dance-drum-and-chant tradition, with paranku frame-drum and odaiko large drum ensembles processing through Okinawan villages during the lunar-Bon mid-August period.",
